beat East Carolina 41-34 in overtime on Thursday night.","story":"MEMPHIS, Tenn. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5165807/marcus-stokes\" target=\"_new\">Marcus Stokes</a> was 29-of-43 passing for 320 yards and three touchdowns and added two rushing TDs to help Memphis beat East Carolina 41-34 in overtime on Thursday night. \n\n\r\n              Stokes’ 5-yard rushing TD on the first possession of OT capped the scoring. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5083052/ellis-ellis-jr\" target=\"_new\">Ellis Ellis Jr</a>. intercepted a pass in the end zone to end the game for Memphis (6-2, 3-1 American Conference). \n\n\r\n              Jermyri Davis had eight receptions for 91 yards and two touchdowns for the Tigers. \n\n\r\n              After Stokes capped a 13-play, 80-yard drive with a 2-yard scoring run with 3:31 left in regulation, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4433829/mitch-griffis\" target=\"_new\">Mitch Griffis</a> threw a 20-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5122006/landon-sides\" target=\"_new\">Landon Sides</a> on fourth-and-9 about 2 minutes later that made it 34-all and forced overtime. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5089443/noah-perez\" target=\"_new\">Noah Perez</a> kicked field goals of 22, 30 and a career-long 49 yards for ECU (3-4, 1-2), the last of which made it 16-3 as time expired in the first half. \n\n\r\n              Griffis replaced starting quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5075800/emory-williams\" target=\"_new\">Emory Williams</a> early in the second quarter and was 14-of-26 passing for 199 yards with a touchdown and two interceptions. Williams finished 5 of 13 for 61 yards passing. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079419/tj-engleman-jr\" target=\"_new\">TJ Engleman Jr</a>. had 92 yards rushing and a TD for the Pirates and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5194306/ashton-gray\" target=\"_new\">Ashton Gray</a> added a 1-yard rushing touchdown. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5264658/jermane-hayes\" target=\"_new\">Jermane Hayes</a> caught a 59-yard scoring strike from Stokes a little more than a minute into the second half that cut the Memphis deficit to 16-10. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              ECU: Hosts Temple on Oct. 31. \n\n\r\n              Memphis: Hosts Army on Halloween. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-23T04:00:13Z"}}